# .trivyignore — findings reviewed and accepted.
#
# One block per finding: what it is, why it is not fixable here, why it is not
# reachable, when to revisit. Cleared waivers are deleted, not kept — git log
# has the history. Default calendar revisit for everything: 2026-11.
#
# Deployment assumptions the "REVERT IF" markers guard: no gRPC monitor, no
# gamedig monitor, no Cloudflare Tunnel monitor, dashboard not reachable from
# untrusted networks, and every MySQL/MariaDB endpoint we connect to (monitor
# targets and the app's own database) sits on our own trusted segment.

# ============================================================================
# uptime-kuma npm deps. `npm ci` installs package-lock.json verbatim, so a
# same-tag rebuild never moves these — only an upstream lockfile change does.
# Overriding the pins downstream would be a source fork, which this repo does
# not do (see oss-mirror-build/README.md).
# ============================================================================

# minimatch ReDoS (HIGH, DoS). Needs an attacker-controlled glob pattern.
# server/ has no minimatch call site.
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# glob CLI command injection (HIGH). Only the `glob -c <cmd>` CLI form is
# affected; uptime-kuma uses the programmatic API and never spawns the CLI.
CVE-2025-64756

# node-tar 6.2.1, extraction path-traversal / hardlink / symlink family
# (HIGH). Fix floor 7.5.11 — a major jump from the `~6.2.1` pin.
# Only require("tar") sites are extra/download-dist.js (install-time) and
# extra/release/lib.mjs (release tooling); not in the server runtime graph.
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802

# node-tar 6.2.1, second wave: gzip-bomb DoS (59873 — NVD says CRITICAL, GHSA
# CVSS is 7.5 A:H, availability only) and an infinite loop in tar.replace()
# (59874). Fixes 7.5.19 / 7.5.18. Same unreachability as the block above;
# tar.replace() is additionally never called anywhere in uptime-kuma.
# REVERT IF: a runtime require("tar") appears upstream.
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874

# node-tar 6.2.1, third wave: DoS via a crafted long-path archive (HIGH).
# Fix floor moves again, now 7.5.21 — still a major jump from the `~6.2.1`
# pin. Same unreachability as the two blocks above, re-verified at 2.5.3:
# the only require("tar") in the tree is extra/download-dist.js:3, which is
# install-time tooling and not in the release image's runtime graph.
# (extra/release/lib.mjs, named in the block above, no longer requires tar.)
CVE-2026-73566

# brace-expansion 1.1.16 (under glob→minimatch@3) + 2.1.2 (under minimatch@9,
# pulled by redbean-node's glob@10): unbounded result length causing an
# uncatchable OOM (14257) and unbounded intermediate arrays that bypass the
# 14257 mitigation (69152). DoS only, both A:H with no confidentiality or
# integrity impact.
# Correction to the earlier note here: the maintenance branches DID get
# backports — 1.1.17/2.1.3 for 14257, 1.1.18/2.1.4 for 69152 — and both are
# inside minimatch's `^1.1.7`/`^2.0.1` ranges. So this is fixable by an
# upstream `npm update`, not by us: package-lock.json pins the old versions
# and we do not fork the lockfile.
# Reachable only through a minimatch/glob pattern. No require("glob") or
# require("minimatch") anywhere in server/, src/ or extra/; the only prod
# consumers are redbean-node's ORM globbing and cacache/node-gyp/rimraf, all
# on literal internal paths. No attacker-controlled pattern reaches expand().
# REVERT IF: upstream adds a glob/minimatch call site fed by user input.
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# socket.io-parser 4.2.6 (under socket.io ~4.8.3) — a crafted packet makes the
# decoder announce binary attachments and buffer reconstructor state that
# never completes; repeated, it exhausts memory (HIGH, CVSS 3.1 A:H only).
# Fix 4.2.7 satisfies socket.io's `~4.2.4` range, so again an upstream
# lockfile refresh closes it; the pin is what blocks us. No workaround exists
# per the advisory (GHSA-2m8v-j782-fhvr).
# Honest exposure — this is the weakest waiver in the file: the decoder sits
# on the dashboard's socket.io endpoint and runs BEFORE authentication.
# server/uptime-kuma-server.js allowRequest() admits every polling connection
# and every websocket without an Origin header, so anyone who can reach the
# port can drive it. Accepted on impact ceiling, not on unreachability: worst
# case is an OOM-kill and a container restart (no code execution, no data
# exposure), and this image's dashboard runs on our internal segment only.
# Same acceptance basis as CVE-2026-48779 carried previously.
# REVERT IF: the dashboard becomes reachable from an untrusted network, or
# upstream refreshes the lockfile — whichever comes first. Re-check every bump.
CVE-2026-69185

# ip-address 10.2.0 (under socks, via socks-proxy-agent and the mongodb
# driver) — Address4 parses a leading-zero octet as decimal while resolvers
# read it as octal, so `012.0.0.1` classifies as public but connects to
# 10.0.0.1 (CVSS 4.0 = 7.7, scored almost entirely on SC:H — the compromised
# security boundary, VC:L/VI:N/VA:N on the vulnerable system itself).
# The entire impact of this CVE is a trust-boundary bypass, and uptime-kuma
# builds no such boundary: no isPrivate/isLoopback/isInSubnet/isLinkLocal call
# anywhere in server/ or src/, and no SSRF filter to bypass. Pointing a
# monitor at an internal host is the product's purpose, and monitor targets
# are admin-supplied through the authenticated UI. socks only uses the parse
# result to choose the SOCKS address type for a connection the operator
# already asked for.
# Fix 10.3.1 is inside socks' `^10.1.1` range — upstream lockfile refresh.
# REVERT IF: uptime-kuma ever adds a target allow/deny list built on
# ip-address; then this becomes a real SSRF bypass rather than a non-issue.
CVE-2026-69192

# protobufjs 7.2.6 — RCE via crafted .proto (41242, CVSS 9.8), plus the
# follow-on family: decode recursion DoS (44289), option-path DoS (44290),
# prototype-pollution codegen gadget (44291, CVSS 8.1), bytes-default code
# injection (44293, CVSS 8.1), and uncontrolled recursion DoS (48712).
# Fix floors 7.5.5 / 7.5.6 / 7.6.1, all outside the `~7.2.6` pin.
# Single call site: server/monitor-types/grpc.js decodes gRPC responses
# against a user-supplied .proto. We run no gRPC monitor, so the decode path
# is never invoked. Even with one, the .proto is admin-supplied via the
# authenticated UI.
# REVERT IF: a gRPC monitor is added — 41242 and 44291 are RCE shapes.
CVE-2026-41242
CVE-2026-44289
CVE-2026-44290
CVE-2026-44291
CVE-2026-44293
CVE-2026-48712

# lodash 4.17.23 (nested under redbean-node; top-level is already 4.18.1) —
# _.template imports key injection (HIGH). redbean-node uses lodash for
# utility functions only; _.template is never invoked.
CVE-2026-4800

# jsonata 2.1.1 — $toMillis resource exhaustion (HIGH, DoS). Fix 2.2.0,
# outside the `~2.1.0` pin. Backs the json-query monitor; the expression is
# admin-supplied via the authenticated UI, only the evaluated data comes from
# the probe target. Worst case is a transient event-loop stall.
CVE-2026-52746

# jsonata 2.1.1, second wave: arbitrary code execution via a crafted JSONata
# EXPRESSION (77413 CVSS 9.8, 77414, 77415 — all CRITICAL). Fix 2.2.1 / 1.8.8,
# outside the `~2.1.0` pin.
# The attacker-controlled input for all three is the expression itself, not
# the data it evaluates over — that is what makes this waivable here. Every
# call site takes the expression from an admin-configured monitor field:
#   server/monitor-types/mongodb.js:27  jsonata(monitor.jsonPath)
#   server/monitor-types/mqtt.js:79,106 jsonata(monitor.jsonPath)
#   src/util.js:409,444                 jsonPath / jsonQueryExpression
# All four are set through the authenticated EditMonitor UI. Only the probe
# RESPONSE is untrusted, and feeding data to an already-parsed expression is
# not the vulnerable path. An operator who can write a monitor expression can
# already reach the server in easier ways.
# REVERT IF: an expression ever becomes derivable from probe output, an API
# payload, or any unauthenticated input. Re-grep the call sites on each bump.
CVE-2026-77413
CVE-2026-77414
CVE-2026-77415

# nodemailer 7.0.13 — message-level `raw` bypasses disableFileAccess /
# disableUrlAccess (HIGH). Fix 9.0.1, two majors out. The smtp provider builds
# messages from admin-configured settings and never exposes `raw`.
# CVE-2026-82659 is the CVE ID for this same GHSA (Trivy now reports the CVE
# form). Not a second finding.
GHSA-p6gq-j5cr-w38f
CVE-2026-82659

# liquidjs 10.26.0 — the `pop` filter skips memoryLimit accounting. Fix
# 10.27.1, outside the `~10.26.0` pin.
# uptime-kuma never configures memoryLimit (no memoryLimit/renderLimit
# anywhere in the tree), so there is no budget to bypass — patched and
# unpatched behave identically here. No template uses `pop`.
# REVERT IF: uptime-kuma starts setting a liquidjs memoryLimit.
CVE-2026-55575

# liquidjs 10.26.0 — infinite loop in the `strip_html` filter (HIGH, DoS).
# Fix 10.27.1, outside the `~10.26.0` pin.
# Unlike 55575 this one IS driven by the filter's input, so unreachability
# rests on the filter never being invoked. The only Liquid engine in the tree
# is server/notification-providers/notification-provider.js:76, rendering
# notification templates; `strip_html` appears in no shipped template and in
# no locale file (grepped across the 2.5.3 tree, zero hits outside
# node_modules). Reaching it needs an admin to write `| strip_html` into a
# custom template by hand, and the ceiling is then an event-loop stall in the
# notification path — no code execution, no data exposure.
# REVERT IF: strip_html appears in a shipped template, or upstream refreshes
# the lockfile.
CVE-2026-61556

# axios 0.32.0 — the Node HTTP adapter can read config.proxy off a polluted
# Object.prototype. Fix 0.33.0 / 1.18.0, outside the `~0.32.0` pin.
# axios IS the HTTP-monitor engine, so this rests on the exploit chain, not on
# the library being unused. It needs a REQUEST interceptor returning a
# plain-object clone; uptime-kuma has none (its only interceptor is a response
# one, server/modules/axios-ntlm/lib/ntlmClient.js:197), so the config
# reaching the adapter is still mergeConfig's null-prototype object. It also
# never sets config.proxy — proxying uses HttpProxyAgent / HttpsProxyAgent /
# SocksProxyAgent from server/proxy.js.
# REVERT IF: any interceptors.request.use appears. Grep on every upstream bump.
# Re-verified at 2.5.3: still no interceptors.request.use in server/, src/ or
# extra/. CVE-2026-67320 is the CVE ID assigned to this same GHSA — Trivy now
# reports the CVE form, so both IDs are listed. Not a second finding.
GHSA-gcfj-64vw-6mp9
CVE-2026-67320

# ws 8.19.0 — memory-exhaustion DoS from small WebSocket fragments (HIGH).
# Fix 8.21.0.
# Scope shrank at 2.5.0: engine.io / engine.io-client / socket.io-adapter now
# resolve ws 8.21.1 and mqtt resolves 7.5.12, all fixed. What remains is the
# top-level `ws@~8.19.0` pin, whose only call site is
# server/monitor-types/websocket-upgrade.js — an OUTBOUND client toward an
# operator-configured probe target. The pre-auth dashboard exposure this entry
# used to carry is gone.
# REVERT IF: a server-side ws listener appears, or ws is used to accept
# inbound connections.
CVE-2026-48779

# @grpc/grpc-js 1.8.22 — malformed request crashes a server (48068), malformed
# compressed message crashes client or server (48069). DoS only.
# uptime-kuma uses grpc-js as a client only; it operates no gRPC server. The
# client path needs an operator to point a gRPC monitor at a hostile endpoint.
CVE-2026-48068
CVE-2026-48069

# mysql2 3.11.5 — a server can send an AuthSwitchRequest for
# `mysql_clear_password` and the client complies without requiring TLS or an
# explicit opt-in, so the configured password goes out in plaintext (HIGH).
# Fix 3.22.0, far outside the `~3.11.5` pin; upstream lockfile refresh only.
# Honest exposure — this is a confidentiality bug with a real path, not an
# unreachable one, so it is accepted on trust boundary rather than on the code
# being unused. Four call sites, in ascending risk:
#   server/embedded-mariadb.js:4  local unix socket, no network, not exposed
#   server/setup-database.js:8    one-time wizard, operator-entered target
#   server/database.js:9          the app's own DB connection
#   server/monitor-types/mysql.js:4  connects to monitor.databaseConnectionString
#     with monitor.radiusPassword — an arbitrary operator-configured endpoint,
#     and the one that actually matters
# Accepted because every MySQL/MariaDB endpoint this instance talks to (monitor
# targets and the app database alike) is on our own segment, so there is no
# hostile server to send the downgrade and no on-path position to MITM it. The
# blast radius if that assumption breaks is one monitor's DB credential, not
# the dashboard.
# REVERT IF: a MySQL/MariaDB monitor is pointed at a host outside our trusted
# segment, or the app database moves to a connection crossing an untrusted
# network. This is the entry to re-read before adding any MySQL monitor.
GHSA-3f6p-5ww8-9rcr

# ============================================================================
# cloudflared (installed from Cloudflare's apt repo). Idle unless a Cloudflare
# Tunnel monitor is configured; we configure none. We cannot bump what it
# vendors without Cloudflare rebuilding the .deb.
# ============================================================================

# Go stdlib 1.26.4 — os.Root symlink-following traversal (HIGH). Fix 1.26.5.
# cloudflared's filesystem operations run on operator- and config-supplied
# paths, never on network-reachable input.
# NOTE: this ID also applied to our own stage-1 healthcheck binary. That
# occurrence is FIXED, not waived — GOLANG_BASE is 1.26.8-bookworm. A
# .trivyignore line cannot scope by binary, so it mutes both.
CVE-2026-39822

# grpc-go v1.81.1 — xDS RBAC authz bypass (~8.2) and panic (~5.9), plus an
# HTTP/2 rapid-reset mitigation bypass (~7.5). Fix 1.82.1.
# Not closable by our nightly apt refresh either: cloudflare/cloudflared@master
# still declares v1.81.1 (checked 2026-07-27). cloudflared is not xDS-managed,
# so the RBAC engine is dead code in it; the rapid-reset bug targets a gRPC
# server, while cloudflared's gRPC use is client-side toward Cloudflare's edge.
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf
# STALE AS OF 2026-09-05: cloudflared now vendors grpc-go v1.83.0, so this
# entry matches nothing. Left in place for this build only so the deploy is
# not gated on the assumption being wrong; delete it once 2.5.3 is green.

# Go stdlib 1.26.4 — the 2026-09 eight-CVE wave, all HIGH, all fixed in 1.26.6:
#   -33818 encoding/asn1 recursion DoS      -56858 html/template XSS
#   -39821 x/net/idna privilege escalation  -56859 encoding/xml recursion DoS
#   -46600 dns/dnsmessage DoS               -56860 net/url quadratic complexity
#   -56853 net/http h2c DoS                 -56862 crypto/tls KeyUpdate DoS
# Waived only for cloudflared, whose Go runtime we cannot bump without
# Cloudflare rebuilding the .deb. Our own healthcheck binary carried the same
# eight IDs and is FIXED, not waived (GOLANG_BASE 1.26.5 -> 1.26.8, see
# dockerfiles/Dockerfile.override). A .trivyignore line cannot scope by binary,
# so these lines unavoidably mute the fixed binary too.
# cloudflared is idle here: no Cloudflare Tunnel monitor is configured, so the
# binary is present on disk but never executed. Even running, the wave is
# DoS/parsing shapes against a client dialling Cloudflare's edge.
# REVERT IF: a Cloudflare Tunnel monitor is configured.
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862

# golang.org/x/crypto v0.53.0 — golang.org/x/crypto/ssh authentication bypass
# from unenforced source-address restrictions (CRITICAL). Fix 0.55.0.
# This is the only CRITICAL in the cloudflared set and the entry to re-check
# first. It is an SSH SERVER-side control: the bug is that a server fails to
# enforce the source-address restriction attached to an authorized key.
# cloudflared vendors x/crypto/ssh for its ssh-proxying feature, which is only
# reached when a tunnel with an ssh ingress rule is running. We run no tunnel
# and no ingress config at all, so no SSH listener is ever started.
# REVERT IF: cloudflared is ever actually run here, in any configuration.
CVE-2026-56854

# google.golang.org/grpc v1.83.0 (HIGH). Fix 1.83.1 — one patch release, but
# still Cloudflare's to ship; we cannot bump a vendored module inside a .deb.
# Supersedes the v1.81.1 entry above. cloudflared's gRPC use is client-side
# toward Cloudflare's edge and is not xDS-managed; idle regardless, per the
# section header.
# REVERT IF: a Cloudflare Tunnel monitor is configured.
CVE-2026-84304
